{
  "name": "v07-keeper-fee-cap",
  "description": "Epoch 1: keeper cost under the cap, K = C; a direct tx counts in full, a publishMany naming three distributors counts one third (floor), a stranger tx, a tx to another distributor and a tx before fromBlock do not count. Epoch 2: cost far above the cap, K = floor(I0 * 2%) and the result lands exactly on the on-chain 2% limit, so no re-cap. Epoch 3: K = floor(I0 * 2%) = 1 but the shares floor to 48, 1 * 10000 > 49 * 200, so K is re-capped to floor(48 * 200 / 9800) = 0 without recomputing shares. Epoch 4: a large epoch (I0 = 1000002) where the cap is 20000; a publishMany naming only other distributors does not count.",
  "covers": [
    "keeper attribution",
    "K = C under the cap",
    "2% cap boundary",
    "re-cap rule",
    "l1 fee in cost"
  ],
